  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x=2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={32}^{\u2218}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\cdot {32}^{\u2218})=2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{32}^{\u2218}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{32}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{64}^{\u2218}=2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{32}^{\u2218}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{32}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nDividing both sides by $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{32}^{\u2218},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{64}^{\u2218}}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{32}^{\u2218}} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{32}^{\u2218}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{32}^{\u2218}}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{32}^{\u2218}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{32}^{\u2218}\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{32}^{\u2218}}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{32}^{\u2218}}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{32}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
